  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human-centred recovery and Decent Work agenda reflected in the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Frameworks and Decent Work Country Programmes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Decent Work Programme (DWP) for the Occupied Palestinian Territory (OPT) 2023-2025 represents a strategic continuation and evolution of the ILO&#x2019;s efforts to support sustainable development, decent work, and socio-economic recovery in the West Bank, Gaza, and East Jerusalem. Building upon the foundations laid by the DWP 2018-2022, this new DWP aligns with the State of Palestine&apos;s ongoing aspirations and challenges, underpinned by the Palestinian National Policy Agenda and aligned to the United Nations Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UNSDCF) 2023&#x2013;2025. 

The DWP 2023-2025 serves as the primary framework for ILO activities in the OPT, emphasizing collaboration between the Palestinian Authority, social partners, and the ILO to advance the Decent Work Agenda and the principles enshrined in the ILO Declaration on Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work. It targets the enhancement of social cohesion, justice, equality, and progress towards the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), particularly SDG 8, which focuses on promoting sustained, inclusive, and sustainable economic growth, full and productive employment, and decent work for all. 
Reflecting a deepened commitment to fostering productive work under conditions of freedom, equity, security, and human dignity, the DWP 2023-2025 prioritizes the facilitation of social dialogue and supports Palestinian tripartite partners&#x2014;including the Ministry of Labour, the Palestine General Federation of Trade Unions (PGFTU), and the Palestinian Federation of Industries (PFCCIA)&#x2014;in becoming more accountable, effective, and representative. 
Aligned with the UNSDCF 2023&#x2013;2025, the DWP introduces three strategic priorities&#x2014;Prosperity, People, and Peace&#x2014;each with specific outcomes designed to address the unique challenges faced by Palestinians: 
